The zib on the patch review workflow records the design and the
reasoning behind it, but parts of it describe tooling that was never
built or that has since changed. An operator who wants to run the
workflow has to piece the real interface together from scripts,
Justfiles on two branches, notmuch hooks and the process-email skill.

This guide collects that interface in one place, for the contributor,
moderator and maintainer roles, taken from the code as it stands. It
opens with one full cycle, from a request on the list to a patch on
trunk, so a reader sees how the roles hand work to each other before
reading the detail of each one.
